# The Theorist, Jace Beleren's -2: "For each opponent, return up to one target artifact or creature that player controls to
# its owner's hand." Bot1 owns Sol Ring; Bot2's kicked Thieving Skydiver takes it (turn 2), so Bot2 controls both Sol Ring
# and the Skydiver. On turn 3 (Jace at 4 after turn 1's +1) the -2 refuses Bot1's own Illusion (it must be a permanent an
# opponent controls) and Bot2's Island (neither an artifact nor a creature). Bot1 targets Sol Ring, and no second target
# is asked for: the Skydiver is Bot2's too, and the ability takes one per opponent. Sol Ring goes to its OWNER's hand -
# Bot1's, not its controller's - while the Skydiver stays, and Jace ends at 2 (CR 400.3, 115.1).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Sol Ring
The Theorist, Jace Beleren
Island x3
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Thieving Skydiver
Island x4
Island x12

